<SddScope keywords="scope, authoring, product, library, sdd-new, sdd-check" type="directive" ver="2.4">
  <Mission>
    Author one product/library scope from durable artifacts, not transcript memory. The autonomous
    route is skeleton → orient → one whole-document Write → soft check → module handoff. The generated skeleton owns
    section format. Module/entity/DbC detail belongs to the module owner.

    **Modes:** greenfield · refine · pivot · rewrite.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_TOOL_INVOCATION">
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-progressive-disclosure"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-pivot-requires-supersession"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <Contracts>
    {{> "contract/process/deviation-record-format"}}
  </Contracts>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_REWRITE_WITH_DOWNSTREAM` | `rewrite` mode but the scope already has module specs or task tickets on disk — not v0, use `pivot` (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`) |
    | `H_PIVOT_NO_INVALIDATION_LIST` | `pivot` mode without a Pivot Invalidation List |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_CREATE">
      <Goal>Create the working artifact before reading optional protocols.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Classify the scope type and mode exactly once from the request and disk. Preserve the
        operator-confirmed `scale:` retained by this owner; must not reopen the already-settled route.
        Greenfield starts with exactly one applicable ToolCall. Existing specs are read in full;
        every mode still produces exactly one whole-document `Write`, authoring never edits them
        section by section. `refine` extends the existing decisions in place. `pivot` replaces a
        decision but never the history: the prior Decision Log entry is preserved byte-for-byte and
        one new entry is appended naming the delta, per `AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`. `rewrite`
        is the v0 exception — no supersession, no invalidation list — and is forbidden once the
        scope already has module specs or task tickets on disk; halt (`H_REWRITE_WITH_DOWNSTREAM`)
        and use `pivot` instead.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="productManifest">npx gennady sdd-new product --scope <scope></ToolCall> Inputs <scope>: request scope classified in this step. Use productManifest.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="libraryManifest">npx gennady sdd-new library --scope <scope></ToolCall> Inputs <scope>: request scope classified in this step. Use libraryManifest.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_1_ORIENT">
      <Goal>Load only the bounded neighbouring context.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="orientation">npx gennady sdd-orient --scope <scope></ToolCall> Inputs <scope>: scope resolved in STEP_0_CREATE. Use orientation.
        This is the only unconditional foreign-context read. Load interview-protocol, rule-registry,
        or research-gate only when the brief or orientation names their trigger. A brief that already
        names the consumer, happy path, negative path, constraints, and exclusions needs no interview.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_2_FILL">
      <Goal>Generate and write the complete specification once.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read the on-disk skeleton once, then compose the COMPLETE document in memory from its section
        order, headings, local comments, and manifest. Replace the skeleton with exactly ONE `Write`
        of the whole file. `Edit`, `Patch`, and per-section writes are forbidden in authoring. The
        one Write must retain every SECTION marker, replace every `<!-- ... -->` guidance comment with
        content, and leave no skeleton guidance behind. Run the structural self-check mentally before
        that Write. Record each disputed autonomous choice once in the scope Decision Log per
        `DEVIATION_RECORD_FORMAT`. In `pivot` mode the same Write also appends the superseded Decision
        Log entry and a Pivot Invalidation List enumerating every downstream module spec/task ticket
        needing `refine-module` or reopening — read
        `ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/pivot-formats.xml` for the exact entry/list format
        (`H_PIVOT_NO_INVALIDATION_LIST` if the list is omitted). Keep scope ownership thin. Do not
        preload structure, requirement, caption, or portal formats.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_3_CHECK">
      <Goal>Consume one mechanical draft receipt.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="draftReceipt">npx gennady sdd-check --spec <scope-spec-path> --authoring</ToolCall> Inputs <scope-spec-path>: exact path from the STEP_0_CREATE manifest. Use draftReceipt.
        The receipt auto-fixes trivial format. If a content hint remains, report authoring incomplete;
        never switch to sectional Edit/Patch repair after the whole-document Write. Rerun once only
        after checker auto-fix to obtain the final receipt. Never raise a draft time limit to
        compensate for reading. Do not run `sdd-check --all specs/<scope>` here:
        before module materialization it is guaranteed to report broken links.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <ScalePath when="scale=function|fix">
      Continue directly into the module owner in the same pass. A small single-purpose scope normally
      becomes exactly one cohesive module. Treat the scope and module manifests as one authoring
      manifest; the scope owns its requirement IDs and the module cites them instead of copying them.
    </ScalePath>

    <Step id="STEP_4_CLOSE">
      <Goal>Make scope authoring completion durable.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Only after the final draftReceipt has no hints, close authoring atomically.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="scopeAuthoringReceipt">npx gennady sdd-log &lt;scope-spec-path&gt; authoring-complete</ToolCall> Inputs &lt;scope-spec-path&gt;: exact checked path from STEP_3_CHECK. Use scopeAuthoringReceipt.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_5_HANDOFF">
      <Goal>Leave a checked actual scope/module set.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Route incomplete decomposition to module authoring. When an operator is actually present and
        explicitly requested interactive review, lazily
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/authoring-interactive.directive.xml")`.
        Autonomous authoring records deviations and continues without Approval/STOP ceremony.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>
</SddScope>
